## 6. Checkpoint: Inbound vs. Outbound Rules

Inbound rules control network traffic coming into a computer. Outbound rules control network traffic leaving the computer. Both help determine which connections Windows Firewall permits or blocks.

## 7. Security Analysis

Firewall rules help control network communication and reduce unauthorized access. An analyst should inspect the rule's direction, enabled status, program or service, and applicable network profiles before determining whether it is appropriate.

An enabled rule does not automatically indicate a security risk, and a disabled rule is not automatically a problem.

